paragraphs.en:
The colour of clouds is called fair, but they often turn dark;
the sound of wind is called clear, but it often stops.
That which is both good and never ceases is water alone, I think.

When it is warm they flower, when it is cold their leaves fall;
pine, how is it that you know nothing of snow and frost?
By that I know your roots run straight down to the Nine Springs.
